Christophe COCHET <cochet@int-evry.fr> wrote:
> Hello,
> Iam looking for some information about UNO and

"Universal Networked Objects" (UNO) is a specification adopted by
the Object Management Group (OMG), as part of it's Common Object
Request Broker (CORBA) specification.

Get a copy of UNO by using the mail server:

    % mail server@omg.org

    send docs/95.3.10.ps
    .
    %

>	particularly I'd like to know 
> the differences between UNO and DCE.

UNO is how CORBA objects interoperate.  It includes bridging
support that allows security firewalls to be built.  It also
allows for the use of DCE to talk to CORBA objects, though it
does not require it.  (There's a requirement for a much lighter
weight protocol, for which a freely licenced, portable, and very
small implementation is already available.)

> Does any product from UNO exist ?

UNO is an OMG specification.  Ask your ORB vendor when their
product will comply with the CORBA 2.0 interoperability spec.
I know several that could provide an implementation in the
next month or so, to suitably qualified customers.

-- 
David Brownell                        db@Eng.Sun.COM.
Enterprise Distributed Objects

