hi,
	I am writing RPC-based server application using Encina and DCE. I 
run into problems such as corrupted stacks and corrupted pthread internal 
data structures. I suspect that they are due to stack overflow of server 
threads.

	The documentation for pthreads says that stack-size must be specified 
at thread creation time. But, the server threads are created by the RPC-runtime
not the application itself. Is there any way I can "instruct" the RPC run-time 
to allocate a larger stack to each thread? 

